    <div class="tg-hero__inner">
      <span class="tg-hero__type">Part II of Five</span>
      <h1 class="tg-hero__title">The Competing Verses</h1>
      <p class="tg-hero__intro">
        Two sets of New Testament texts appear to say opposite things about whether a
        believer can be lost. Most treatments quote one set and explain the other away.
        This part does neither. It lays both out in full, reads the six hardest
        passages closely in their own contexts, sets out the five standard ways of
        holding them together with the price each one pays — and then looks at the
        verses that were written to be read in pairs.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="tg-hero__key-verse">
        <p>Work out your own salvation with fear and trembling, <strong>for</strong> it
           is God who works in you, both to will and to work for his good pleasure.</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="Philippians 2:12-13">Philippians 2:12–13</a></cite>
      </blockquote>
